    <decisions>
        <name>DEC_Check_if_Meeting_Type_is_Changed</name>
        <label>DEC Check if Meeting Type is Changed</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>END_ELEMENT_4</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Meeting_Type_is_Changed</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>GET_Event_Details.MeetingType__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>meetingType</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Event_with_Meeting_Type</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Meeting Type is Changed</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Routes the two callers apart so neither can overwrite the other&apos;s fields - an internal notes save must never blank Note__c or Published__c. Branches on the explicit saveMode that Apex sends, NOT on which inputs are blank: Flow cannot distinguish an unset variable from an empty string, so inferring the caller would misroute the case where an advisor clears their internal notes and saves.</description>
        <name>DEC_Save_Mode</name>
        <label>DEC Save Mode</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>DEC_Check_if_New_or_Updating_Meeting_Note</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Meeting Summary Save</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Internal_Notes_Only</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>saveMode</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>internalNotes</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>DEC_Internal_New_or_Update</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Internal Notes Only</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Create only when no note exists at all - see formResolvedNoteId, which also consults Event.MeetingNote__c so a blank noteId cannot produce a duplicate.</description>
        <name>DEC_Check_if_New_or_Updating_Meeting_Note</name>
        <label>DEC Check if New or Updating Meeting Note</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>ASN_Summary_Existing_Note_Id</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Update Meeting Note</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Create_Meeting_Note</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>formResolvedNoteId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsBlank</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Create_MeetingNote</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Create Meeting Note</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Same create-or-update test as the summary branch, using the same resolved id so both callers converge on one MeetingNote__c per Event.</description>
        <name>DEC_Internal_New_or_Update</name>
        <label>DEC Internal New or Update</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>ASN_Internal_Existing_Note_Id</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Update Internal Notes</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Create_Note_For_Internal_Notes</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>formResolvedNoteId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsBlank</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Create_MeetingNote_Internal</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Create Note For Internal Notes</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Saves a MeetingNote__c for the Advisor Assistant component. Serves two callers: MeetingSummaryController.saveMeetingNote (summary, brief, published, meeting type) and MeetingSummaryController.saveInternalNotes (Internal_Notes__c only). Returns savedNoteId in both cases, which the component relies on to avoid creating duplicate notes.</description>
    <ends>
        <name>END_ELEMENT_4</name>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
    </ends>
    <ends>
        <name>END_ELEMENT_5</name>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
    </ends>
    <ends>
        <name>END_ELEMENT_6</name>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
    </ends>
    <ends>
        <name>END_ELEMENT_7</name>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
    </ends>
    <ends>
        <name>END_ELEMENT_8</name>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
    </ends>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>formMeetingNoteName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>LEFT({!GET_Event_Details.Subject} &amp; &quot; / &quot; &amp; TEXT({!GET_Event_Details.EndDate}), 80)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>The note record to write to. Prefers the id the component passed; falls back to the note already linked on the Event. That fallback is the duplicate guard: if the component ever sends a blank noteId for an Event that already has a note, this resolves to the existing record instead of creating a second one. Blank here genuinely means no note exists yet.</description>
        <name>formResolvedNoteId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!noteId}), {!GET_Event_Details.MeetingNote__c}, {!noteId})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>WealthPlan - AL - Meeting Summary Save/Update {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>WealthPlan - AL - Meeting Summary Save/Update</label>
